    {
      "obligation": "refuter:17:1",
      "id": "thm-a-riemannian-metric-has-a-unique-levi-civita-connection-on-the-cotangent-bundle",
      "location": "4.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "The cited definition says a connection is “symmetric when $\\Gamma^k_{ij}=\\Gamma^k_{ji}$ in every chart” and metric-compatible when its formula holds “in every chart.” Steps 1.1–2.2 fix one chart and establish those equations only there. Step 4.1 then says the locally constructed operators agree on overlaps “because both are symmetric and metric-compatible,” but it neither proves nor cites the required Christoffel-symbol transformation/invariance argument showing that the operator constructed in one chart has those properties when expressed in the other. Thus step 3.1 cannot yet be applied to compare the two local constructions, so the global gluing conclusion is unsupported.",
      "severity": "fatal",
